/* Partitioned overlap-save convolution, reference profile: double-double.
 *
 * Every value is a DoubleDoubleComplex, four doubles, so this bank is twice
 * the footprint of the FP64 one and each product costs a dozen error-free
 * transformations.  It exists to be the numerical reference the other
 * profiles are measured against, not to be fast.  The device must report
 * shaderFloat64; double_double.glsl states the rules that keep the compiler
 * from folding the compensation terms away.
 *
 * Bindings, in the order create_partition_pipeline() writes them:
 *   0 working  -- out: this block's accumulated spectrum.
 *   1 history  -- in: ring of the last `partitions` input spectra per channel.
 *   2 kernels  -- in: the transformed response, partition-major.
 *
 * Push constants (partition_parameters_t, 16 bytes): spectrum_bins,
 * partitions, channels, current_slot.
 *
 * Dispatch covers channels * spectrum_bins invocations rounded up to whole
 * workgroups of 256, hence the bounds test.
 *
